v0.2.0:
    - Added plot saving with Ghostscript
    - Renamed Parameter.constraint to Parameter.setting
    - Various small fixes

v0.2.1:
    - Configuration is now settable during runtime

v0.3.0:
    - New Model class
    - AVLWrapper can now read an AVL input-file

v0.3.1:
    - Merged bufixes from Dario Isola & Phil Chiu

v0.3.2:
    - Bugfix for AIRFOIL keyword

v0.3.3:
    - Lots of bugfixes:
        - Creating Body while parsing inputfiles
        - RegEx bug in ElementFileReader (Thomas Greenhill)
        - Handling large numbers in tables
        - Handling stripforces with index > 99
        - Missing values now replaced with NaN instead of messing up the table format
          (columns were incorrectly shifted in previous versions)
        - Name labels incorrectly read in SurfaceFileReader
        - Type errors (mixing up floats & ints) while reading and writing files
          (AVL usually handles correcntly, but huge gain for consistency)
    - Case can now be read from input file
    - Spacing now parsed correctly
    - Two Spacials can now be added
    - Spacial can be multiplied/divived with a number
    - Added _underscore to separate control name from derivative (CYuelevator => CYu_elevator)
    - Added tests cases

v0.3.4:
    - Support multiple cases in 1 input file
    - Added body forces output
  ! - Cases are now indexed by number instead of name, since names are not required to be unique

v0.4.0:
    - Added mass distribution input
    - Added eigen-mode analysis and system matrix output

V0.4.1:
    - Lots of bugfixes:
        - Profile drag (CDCL) on more than one section was dropped or crashed
          while parsing input files
        - Negative masses were dropped while parsing mass files
        - Mass modifiers on masses without inertia
        - Malformed BODY header now raises an InputError
        - Unreadable error messages of InputError
        - Configuration.local_copy() now copies to the current working directory
        - Ghostscript output path
    - importing avlwrapper no longer requires tkinter
    - Single exception hierarchy, available as avlwrapper.AvlError, InputError,
      AvlExecutionError and OutputError
    - AVL failures are detected and raise an AvlExecutionError with the AVL output
    - Session accepts a timeout
    - Plots can be saved to a directory with the output_dir argument
    - Added Case.validate(), a Case can be printed without a Session
  ! - Session no longer modifies the given cases, use Session.cases to get the
      cases as used in the run
  ! - Unknown keywords in a Case which are not a control of the geometry now
      raise an InputError when running the Session
  ! - Eigenvalues are now indexed by case number as int instead of str
  ! - The AVL executable is no longer searched for in sys.path
  ! - PrintOutput prints the AVL output after the run instead of during the run

v0.5.0:
    - Results are read from AVL's full-precision machine-readable output (MRF)
    - Added Options to set AVL's axes, profile drag, trailing-leg forces and
      body-induced velocities: Session(..., options=Options(...))
    - AINC keyword (alternative for ANGLE) in input files
    - Eigenvectors: run_mode_analysis() returns "EigenModes"
    - Mode analysis of selected cases: run_mode_analysis(cases=[...])
    - Session.mass_properties(): mass, CG, inertia and apparent mass
    - Trimmed cases: Case(..., trim=Trim.level_flight) or Trim.looping
    - Results contain the solved "States" of each case (alpha, CL, velocity, ...)
    - Off-body flow survey: Session(..., survey_points=[...])
    - Surface pressures on the outer mould lines (SurfacePressures output)
    - Strip forces in body axes (StripForcesBodyAxes output)
    - Design changes: Session(..., design_changes={"twist": 1.5})
    - Tests run in CI against AVL 3.52 built from source (ci/build-avl.sh)
    - Tests which need AVL are skipped when it's not installed
  ! - Requires AVL 3.40 or later. The version is checked before AVL is used
      for the first time, an older version raises an AvlVersionError
  ! - The readers of AVL's regular (formatted) output files are removed, the
      outputs of the OPER menu have to be in the machine-readable format
  ! - Results have full precision instead of the 4 to 6 digits in AVL's
      regular output
  ! - Derivatives with respect to design variables are named after the
      variable (CL_twist instead of CLg01)
  ! - Centre of pressure (C.P.x/c) of strips without lift is AVL's computed
      value instead of 999
  ! - Requires Python 3.11 or later (already the case since 0.4.0)
  ! - Mode analysis results are indexed by case number, also the
      SystemMatrix (which held only the first case)

v0.6.0:
    - Results are read-only mappings with attributes, e.g.
      results[1].totals["CLtot"], results.by_name("cruise") and to_dict()
    - Eigenmodes with complex eigenvalue and eigenvector, natural frequency,
      damping ratio, period and time to half/double the amplitude
    - Outputs are selected in the code: Options(outputs={Output.TOTALS, ...})
    - Configuration looks for config.cfg in the working directory, then in the
      user's configuration directory; AVL_EXECUTABLE environment variable
  ! - The [output] section of config.cfg is ignored, with a deprecation
      warning. Select the outputs with Options(outputs=...)
  ! - Configuration is a settings object: Configuration(avl_executable=...),
      Configuration.from_file(path), config.avl_path, config.ghostscript_path
      and config.print_output replace config["avl_bin"], config.settings, ...
  ! - Mode analysis results are by case number first:
      modes[1].eigenvalues instead of modes["EigenValues"][1]
  ! - Eigenvalues and eigenvectors are complex numbers instead of tuples
  ! - Session.OUTPUTS and Session.MODE_OUTPUTS are removed, see avl.Output
